The selectrs package as a whole is distributed under the 3-clause BSD
licence recorded in DESCRIPTION and the file LICENCE. Some of the code
it bundles is under other licences, which this file summarises; the
authoritative list, with the version, licence, authors and repository of
every component, is inst/AUTHORS.

R code, documentation and tests
------------------------------

R/, man/, tests/testthat/ and inst/demos/ are ports of the selectr
package, itself a translation of the Python package cssselect. Both are
3-clause BSD, the same licence as this package.

Vendored Rust crates
--------------------

The Rust core is statically linked from the crates vendored in the
source tarball as src/rust/vendor.tar.xz, at the versions pinned in
src/rust/Cargo.lock. Most are MIT, Apache-2.0, or dual MIT OR
Apache-2.0. The exceptions are:

  cssparser, cssparser-macros, dtoa-short, selectors
      Mozilla Public License 2.0. The MPL requires that the source of
      these files be available: it is, in src/rust/vendor.tar.xz, at the
      versions the shipped object is built from.

  unicode-ident
      (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND Unicode-3.0, the latter covering the
      Unicode character tables the crate embeds.

Licence texts are in each crate's directory inside the vendored archive.
